# CryptoCards scheduled jobs (container-local cron).
#
# Times are container-local. The price engine runs every 12h, staggered so the
# two upstreams aren't hit simultaneously and so a slow run never overlaps itself.
#
# NOTE: price-sync runs WITHOUT --apply. It journals proposals and changes nothing.
# Once you have read a couple of weeks of `make price-report` and trust it, add
# --apply to the two price lines below.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# --- currency rates: 00:05 and 12:05 ---------------------------------------
# Runs BEFORE the price engine, because both read the same Bank of Canada rate
# and a stale conversion_rate mis-prices every USD order. The Bank publishes once
# per business day (~16:30 ET); running twice daily keeps the storefront within
# one publication of the real rate, and the script falls back to the last cached
# rate if Valet is unreachable rather than leaving prices wrong.
5 0,12 * * * www-data php /provisioning/pricing/currency-sync.php >> /var/log/cryptocards-currency.log 2>&1

# --- price engine: 00:15 and 12:15 -----------------------------------------
15 0,12 * * * www-data php /provisioning/pricing/price-sync.php >> /var/log/cryptocards-price.log 2>&1

# --- reindex search after pricing settles -----------------------------------
45 0,12 * * * www-data php /provisioning/catalog/search-index.php >> /var/log/cryptocards-search.log 2>&1

# --- release expired copy reservations, every 5 minutes ---------------------
# An abandoned cart holding a one-of-one card takes it off sale silently: no error
# is raised, the card just stops being available. This is the only thing that
# returns it, so it runs often.
*/5 * * * * www-data php /provisioning/inventory/copies-release.php >> /var/log/cryptocards-copies.log 2>&1

# Database backups are deliberately NOT here: they belong on the host, where the
# dump survives `docker compose down -v`. Use `make backup`, or a host cron
# calling it.
